            ("Does a shiny sauce always count as nappé?", "Shine and body are not the same thing. A thin jus can glint under the lamp and still run to the rim. A starch slurry can thicken until the spoon is coated and still look dull. Nappé is the coat on the spoon, read together with the surface the dish is supposed to have. A reduction and a good roux keep a gloss that a slurry tends to knock back."),
